ADS-016 — Serialization Model

Document ID: ADS-016
Title: Serialization Model
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Serialization Model (CSM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Serialization Model establishes technology-independent principles for representing Canonical Atlas Objects in serialized forms suitable for storage, communication, persistence, interoperability, and archival while preserving semantic integrity.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Serialization architecture
Representation principles
Encoding independence
Schema evolution
Compatibility
Validation
Interoperability
Governance

This specification applies to every serialized representation of Canonical Atlas Objects.

3. Canonical Definition

Serialization is the reversible transformation of a Canonical Atlas Object into a representation suitable for storage or transmission without altering its semantic meaning.

Serialization changes representation.

It SHALL NOT change meaning.

4. Objectives

The Serialization Model SHALL:

Preserve semantics.
Enable interoperability.
Support multiple encodings.
Support schema evolution.
Preserve object identity.
Preserve provenance.
Support validation.
Support long-term archival.
5. Serialization Principles

Every Atlas serialization SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Semantic Preservation

Serialization SHALL preserve canonical semantics.

Reversibility

Deserialization SHALL reconstruct an equivalent Canonical Atlas Object.

Technology Independence

Serialization SHALL NOT depend upon any specific encoding technology.

Determinism

Equivalent objects SHALL produce equivalent serialized representations under the same serialization profile.

Version Awareness

Serialized representations SHALL identify applicable schema versions.

Interoperability

Serialized forms SHALL be exchangeable between conforming implementations.

